**Issue**: #415
**Date**: 2026-09-23
**Status**: Approved
**Author**: NMG

Feature: Reconcile an independently merged spec PR despite local CLI failure
  Publication is determined by the exact remote PR, not GitHub CLI's local checkout result.

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: Merge succeeds remotely but local CLI exits unsuccessfully
    Given an approved spec-only PR passed exact-head readiness at head H on branch B targeting base D
    And the merge CLI remotely merges that PR but exits nonzero during local checkout
    When publication inspects the same PR and proves MERGED at H from B to D
    Then the result includes merged true and that PR number
    And no second merge is attempted

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: A CLI failure without exact remote proof remains pre-merge
    Given a merge CLI failure for an approved spec PR
    But that PR is open, unreadable, or reports a different head or branch identity
    When publication classifies the failure
    Then the result does not claim merged true
    And no spec-created label is applied

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario: Other worktree owns the default branch
    Given the exact PR merged remotely while another worktree owns the default branch
    When local checkout fails and publication reconciles
    Then it reports default_checkout_failed with merged true and the PR number
    And safe independent labeling completes without altering either worktree

  @SCN004 @regression
  Scenario: Repeated publication after a proven merge
    Given the exact spec PR is already merged remotely
    When publication is invoked again from the spec branch
    Then it reports the same merged PR and resumes only incomplete bookkeeping
    And no duplicate PR is created and no merge is reissued
